From 8b144d02bfb9021635763c7be93d5637e7b35227 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:10:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-131: the Events tab with several selected -- the
 events they all have, one handler for all of them (0.131.0)

BCB6's Object Inspector / the Windows Forms designer: with several selected the Events tab
used to show the primary one's events only, and a change went to it alone.
- extension.js resolve: with several selected, the event grid keeps only the events every one
  has; a row whose handlers differ is marked mixed; a .dfm one (golden) or a page-script one
  among them makes the row read only.
- cmdEventMany: a name typed = that function for all -- made once (or the class's own used),
  then each control wired (its page line, its generated-table row); blank Enter / a double
  click = the default name; resetMany: Reset takes every one's designer wiring off, the C++ stays.
- props.js: mixed rows empty with the (different) placeholder; the section says how many in
  common; the menu's Reset says it is all of them, its jump is off on a mixed row.
- tests: smoke (spbSave + sbtExit), panels render (mixed row, Enter, menu); the fake records
  status-bar messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
